1. Accessing Strings
-> Strings are sequences of characters — you can access each character using indexing.

Example:

my_str = "Python"
print(my_str[0])   # Access first character
print(my_str[3])   # Access 4th character (index starts from 0)
print(my_str[-1])  # Access last character


Output:
P
h
n


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


2. Manipulating Strings
-> Concatenation (Joining Strings)

Use the + operator to join two or more strings.

Example:

first = "Data"
second = "Science"
result = first + " " + second
print(result)


Output:

Data Science

-> Repetition

Use the * operator to repeat a string multiple times.

Example:

word = "Hi! "
print(word * 3)


Output:

Hi! Hi! Hi!


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


3. String Methods (Built-in Functions)
-> Method	Description	Example	Output
.upper()	Converts to uppercase	"hello".upper()	"HELLO"
.lower()	Converts to lowercase	"HELLO".lower()	"hello"
.title()	Capitalizes each word	"python language".title()	"Python Language"
.strip()	Removes extra spaces	" data ".strip()	"data"
.replace(a, b)	Replaces substring	"python".replace("py", "my")	"mython"
.find("x")	Finds index of substring	"python".find("t")	2
.count("x")	Counts occurrences	"banana".count("a")	3
.split()	Splits string into list	"a,b,c".split(",")	['a','b','c']


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


4. String Slicing
-> Slicing lets you extract a portion (substring) of a string.

Syntax:

string[start:end:step]


start → index to begin from (included)

end → index to stop before (excluded)

step → how many characters to skip (optional)

Examples:

text = "PythonProgramming"

print(text[0:6])      # 'Python' (from index 0 to 5)
print(text[6:])       # 'Programming' (from 6 to end)
print(text[:6])       # 'Python' (from start to 5)
print(text[::2])      # 'Pto rgamn' (every 2nd character)
print(text[::-1])     